# Chem quiz content

Source of truth is `questions.json` plus `CHAPTER_META`. Do not hand-edit generated `public/quiz/**/js/quizData.js`.

## New topic

In `scripts/quiz/microscopic-world-i/build_quiz.py`, add to `CHAPTER_META`:

```python
9: ("acids-bases", "Acids and Bases", "酸與鹼", "acid"),
```

Tuple is `(sectionId, English label, 繁中 label, id prefix)`. `"ch"` in JSON must be that integer key (`9` here). `id prefix` plus `"n"` becomes `acid-1`.

Update the `len(data) != 40` check to the new total. If `write_manifest` still assumes `"count": 10` per chapter, set it to the real count for each chapter.

## New question

Append in `scripts/quiz/microscopic-world-i/questions.json`:

```json
{
  "ch": 9,
  "n": 1,
  "stem": "Question in English",
  "stemZh": "繁體中文題目",
  "options": ["Option A", "Option B", "Option C", "Option D"],
  "answer": "B",
  "hint": "Brief explanation"
}
```

`options` is four strings, not `{ key, text }` objects. Optional `"image"` only if `FIGURE_FILES` in `build_quiz.py` already maps that key and the file is in `scripts/quiz/microscopic-world-i/figures/`.

Then run:

```bash
python3 scripts/quiz/microscopic-world-i/build_quiz.py
python3 scripts/quiz/microscopic-world-i/validate.py
```

## Remove a topic

Delete those questions from `questions.json`, remove the `CHAPTER_META` row, fix the expected count, rebuild, then commit source + generated `quizData.js` together.
